METHOD
For every half-level 1<=K<=8, the audit exhausts every nonzero integer
profile with coefficients in {0,1,2,3,4,5,6}.  It retains profiles
with positive vacuum coefficient, log-concavity with interval support,
and every nonnegative simple-current boundary.  It constructs the full
finite multiplication matrix and finds the least order of a negative
principal minor by exact fraction-free integer elimination.

Among the profiles with a negative anchored current, 3,630 first fail
PSD at order two and 36 first fail at order three.  No negative-current
profile is PSD.  The audit separately retains all 3,320 PSD profiles
and checks every irreducible-square insertion; none has a negative
output boundary.  All 1,222,078 output anchored-current coordinates
are also nonnegative.  It independently checks the exact identity
`B_R(N_Q^2d)=(N_dz^(m))_R` at all 155,030 profile-factor-radius
coordinates and finds no mismatch.

The audit checks the exact wall-reflection identity at 56,997
coordinates.  It finds no identity mismatch and four negative values
of the tempting separated mixed-boundary subpayment.  The first is the
exact PSD profile `(2,3,4,1)` recorded above; its no-wall compensation
makes the complete wall current positive.

It also tests ordinary unimodality of every residual-column ratio.
There are 4,191 failures among 23,690 columns; the first exact profile
and residual are recorded above.  Thus neither the wall split nor
one-crossing residual ratios replace the complete transport payment.
Natural-order exact `LDL^T` factorization likewise has a negative
off-diagonal multiplier for 385 PSD anchored matrices.

For the exact row-payment identity, the audit checks individual shells,
ordinary initial cumulative sums, mirror shell pairs, and the complete
block.  The first three local strengthenings all have exact failures;
the complete insertion block has none.  These are bounded results for
PSD boundary reduction and PSD boundary insertion, not unbounded
proofs.

